{"id":"b9","level":3,"levelName":"Ulpan Bet","n":19,"of":22,"title":"Saying no","titleHe":"שְׁלִילָה","goal":"Negate a verb, an existence, and a whole idea.","sections":[{"type":"text","body":"לֹא goes before the verb and negates it. אֵין negates existence. They aren't interchangeable: אֲנִי לֹא רוֹאֶה is I don't see, but אֵין סֵפֶר is there's no book."},{"type":"examples","items":[{"he":"אֲנִי לֹא יוֹדֵעַ.","en":"I don't know."},{"he":"אֵין לִי כֶּסֶף.","en":"I have no money."},{"he":"אַף אֶחָד לֹא בָּא.","en":"Nobody came."},{"he":"אַף פַּעַם לֹא הָיִיתִי שָׁם.","en":"I've never been there."}]},{"type":"tip","body":"Hebrew doubles its negatives and means it. אַף אֶחָד לֹא בָּא is literally nobody didn't come, and means nobody came. Dropping the לֹא is wrong."}],"vocab":[{"he":"לֹא","en":"no, not","translit":"lo"},{"he":"אַף אֶחָד","en":"nobody","translit":"af echad"},{"he":"אַף פַּעַם","en":"never","translit":"af pa'am"},{"he":"כְּלוּם","en":"nothing","translit":"klum"},{"he":"עֲדַיִן לֹא","en":"not yet","translit":"adayin lo"},{"he":"רַק","en":"only","translit":"rak"}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["street","awe, fear","no, not","these"],"correct":2,"prompt":"לֹא","translit":"lo"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["nobody","youth, boy","knowledge","houses"],"correct":0,"prompt":"אַף אֶחָד","translit":"af echad"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["gifts of food sent at Purim","never","to me","broken"],"correct":1,"prompt":"אַף פַּעַם","translit":"af pa'am"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["nothing","almost","alone","cupboard, wardrobe"],"correct":0,"prompt":"כְּלוּם","translit":"klum"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["despite","cooks","not yet","was (m.)"],"correct":2,"prompt":"עֲדַיִן לֹא","translit":"adayin lo"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["only","initials, abbreviation","priest","restaurant"],"correct":0,"prompt":"רַק","translit":"rak"},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “nobody”?","options":["לַיְלָה טוֹב","אַף אֶחָד","מְנַקֶּה","כֶּתֶר"],"correct":1,"he":true},{"type":"read","he":"כְּלוּם","translit":"klum","en":"nothing"},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “nothing”?","options":["כְּלוּם","לָשֶׁבֶת","נַחֲלָה","רֹאשׁ הַשָּׁנָה"],"correct":0,"he":true},{"type":"match","pairs":[["לֹא","no, not"],["אַף אֶחָד","nobody"],["אַף פַּעַם","never"],["כְּלוּם","nothing"],["עֲדַיִן לֹא","not yet"]]},{"type":"choice","q":"“Nobody came” —","options":["אַף אֶחָד לֹא בָּא","אַף אֶחָד בָּא","לֹא אַף אֶחָד בָּא","אֵין אֶחָד בָּא"],"correct":0,"why":"The negative word and לֹא both appear; Hebrew requires the double negative."},{"type":"listen","q":"Which word did you hear?","options":["אַף פַּעַם","עֲדַיִן לֹא","לֹא","אַף אֶחָד"],"correct":3,"say":"אַף אֶחָד","he":true},{"type":"listen","q":"Which word did you hear?","options":["כְּלוּם","לֹא","אַף פַּעַם","עֲדַיִן לֹא"],"correct":3,"say":"עֲדַיִן לֹא","he":true},{"type":"cloze","sentence":"אֵין לִי ___.","en":"I have no money.","options":["אַף אֶחָד","כֶּסֶף","עֲדַיִן לֹא","לֹא"],"correct":1,"full":"אֵין לִי כֶּסֶף."},{"type":"cloze","sentence":"אַף פַּעַם לֹא ___ שָׁם.","en":"I've never been there.","options":["אַף אֶחָד","אַף פַּעַם","הָיִיתִי","רַק"],"correct":2,"full":"אַף פַּעַם לֹא הָיִיתִי שָׁם."},{"type":"type","q":"Write “never” in Hebrew","answer":"אַף פַּעַם","hint":"af pa'am"}]}